From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <mk@verveflux.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Feb 2026 08:11:34 +0530
Subject: Use accessor properties for override properties on prototypes

InstallOverrideProperty used SetNativeDataProperty to add properties
like globalPrivacyControl, mozConnection, webkitConnection to
Navigator.prototype. This creates data properties, but native browser
properties are accessor properties with get/set descriptors. Prototype
lie detectors check that accessing the property on the prototype throws
TypeError (native getter behavior) and that the getter is a native
function.

Add InstallOverrideAccessorProperty which installs a proper accessor
property with a FunctionTemplate+RemovePrototype getter that:
- Throws TypeError("Illegal invocation") when called on the prototype
- Has correct "get propName" naming matching native accessors
- Passes all prototype lie detection checks

Keep InstallOverrideProperty for non-prototype targets (Error, process.env)
where data property semantics are appropriate.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/v8_builtin_overrides.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/v8_builtin_overrides.cc
index 67099b321e5dcaf34a1112d8f8ecf3ae0ffde7fc..b2365cfad4c71262973146a8b5605b7e8ac0b650 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/v8_builtin_overrides.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/v8_builtin_overrides.cc
